---
const columns = [
  "Kampa",
  "ChatGPT free",
  "Jasper",
  "HubSpot Campaign Assistant",
];

const rows = [
  {
    label: "Complete 90-day campaign package",
    cells: [
      "yes",
      "blank prompt, you assemble",
      "assets only, no strategy",
      "landing page + email + ad copy only",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "Plans within your budget & hours",
    cells: ["yes", "if you know to ask", "no", "no"],
  },
  {
    label: "Cost",
    cells: [
      "~€1/campaign (your API key)",
      "free but unstructured",
      "€59-69/mo",
      "free, but funnels to €20-890/mo",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "Signup required",
    cells: ["none", "account", "account + card", "HubSpot account"],
  },
  {
    label: "Your data stored on their servers",
    cells: ["no — browser only", "yes", "yes", "yes"],
  },
  {
    label: "Export you own (md/PDF/ics)",
    cells: ["yes", "copy-paste", "limited", "limited"],
  },
];
---

<section class="px-6 py-24 sm:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <h2
      class="max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-balance text-neutral-950 sm:text-5xl"
    >
      Why not just ChatGPT?
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose text-lg text-neutral-600">
      Fair question. Here's the honest answer.
    </p>

    <div
      class="mt-12 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white"
    >
      <table class="w-full min-w-3xl border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-neutral-200">
            <th scope="col" class="w-56 px-5 py-4">
              <span class="sr-only">Capability</span>
            </th>
            {
              columns.map((name, i) => (
                <th
                  scope="col"
                  class:list={[
                    "px-5 py-4 font-semibold",
                    i === 0 ? "text-primary bg-primary/5" : "text-neutral-500",
                  ]}
                >
                  {name}
                </th>
              ))
            }
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            rows.map((row) => (
              <tr class="border-b border-neutral-200 last:border-0">
                <th
                  scope="row"
                  class="px-5 py-4 align-top font-semibold text-neutral-950"
                >
                  {row.label}
                </th>
                {row.cells.map((cell, i) => (
                  <td
                    class:list={[
                      "px-5 py-4 align-top",
                      i === 0
                        ? "bg-primary/5 font-medium text-neutral-950"
                        : "text-neutral-600",
                    ]}
                  >
                    {cell}
                  </td>
                ))}
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 max-w-prose text-base text-neutral-600">
      You could build this yourself in ChatGPT with the right 15 prompts. Kampa
      is those prompts, in the right order, with your constraints enforced and
      the output packaged. That's the whole product — and it's why it's free.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
